  "summary": "CLI tooling with benign network and base64 patterns",
  "details": "Package is a CLI with agent/skill templates and services. Pattern matches cluster in test files and template scripts: curl/wget/ping tokens appear in test fixtures (codex-pre-tool-hook-template.test.js, codex-pre-tool-policy-template.js) that document allowed/forbidden command examples including placeholder hosts like evil.test and example.com, consistent with safety-guardrail prompt text and policy test cases rather than live network calls. Buffer.from(..., 'base64').toString() usage in global-codex-config.js and consumer-release-preparation.mjs is standard base64 decoding of configuration/content, not evaluated as code. api-mcp-runtime.mjs contains ping/GET/POST tokens within a runtime helper. No lifecycle install scripts are implicated, no hardcoded attacker C2 endpoint, no credential or home-directory enumeration, and no fetch-and-execute flow is present in the matched locations.",
